## Issue

`bsmote_impl()` in `R/bsmote_impl.R` uses non-idiomatic boolean comparisons and two separate `if` statements instead of `if`/`else`:

```r
if (all_neighbors == FALSE) {
  tmp_df <- as.data.frame(
    smote_data(
      data = data_mat[min_class_in, ],
      ...
    )
  )
}
if (all_neighbors == TRUE) {
  tmp_df <- as.data.frame(
    smote_data(data_mat, k, samples_needed[i], which(danger_ids))
  )
}
```

Two issues here:

1. `== FALSE` / `== TRUE` should be `!all_neighbors` / `all_neighbors`.
2. Both `if` blocks are always evaluated. If the first runs and sets `tmp_df`, the second `if` is still checked. An `if`/`else` makes the intent clear and avoids the unnecessary second condition check.

## Fix

```r
if (!all_neighbors) {
  tmp_df <- as.data.frame(
    smote_data(
      data = data_mat[min_class_in, ],
      k = k,
      n_samples = samples_needed[i],
      smote_ids = which(danger_ids[min_class_in])
    )
  )
} else {
  tmp_df <- as.data.frame(
    smote_data(data_mat, k, samples_needed[i], which(danger_ids))
  )
}
```

## Issue

`check_numeric()` in `R/misc.R` does not accept or forward a `call` argument to `cli::cli_abort()`. This means errors from this check are attributed to the wrong function in the error message, making them harder to understand for users.

## Current behaviour

```r
check_numeric <- function(dat) {
  all_good <- vapply(dat, is.numeric, logical(1))
  if (!all(all_good)) {
    cli::cli_abort("All columns for this function should be numeric.")
    # No call = argument — error does not point to the user-facing function
  }
}
```

All other check functions in `misc.R` correctly accept and forward `call`:

```r
check_na <- function(data, step, call = caller_env()) { ... cli_abort(..., call = call) }
check_column_factor <- function(data, column, call = caller_env()) { ... cli_abort(..., call = call) }
check_var <- function(var, df, call = caller_env()) { ... cli_abort(..., call = call) }
# etc.
```

## Fix

Update `check_numeric()` to follow the same pattern:

```r
check_numeric <- function(dat, call = caller_env()) {
  all_good <- vapply(dat, is.numeric, logical(1))
  if (!all(all_good)) {
    cli::cli_abort("All columns for this function should be numeric.", call = call)
  }
  invisible(all_good)
}
```

Update all call sites (in `smote_impl.R`, `bsmote_impl.R`, `adasyn_impl.R`, `nearmiss_impl.R`) to pass `call = caller_env()` or `call = call` as appropriate.

